-- title:
--   Drinfeld chart image of y and comaps of its powers
-- statement:
--   **Global data.** Fix a prime $q$ with $5 \le q$, a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell$ with $3 \le \ell$, $\ell \ne q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$. Fix a field $L$ of characteristic zero, an element $\xi \in L$ which is a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity, and assume (`hι`) that there is a ring homomorphism $\iota \colon L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\xi) = \exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ which, by `hK`, equals [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q*ℓ) M'))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103): the subfield generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise images under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) (the map induced by $\mathbb{Q} \to L$) of the intermediate field [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79) of level $(q\ell)^2M'$ attached to the subgroup [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q*ℓ) M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22), namely the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/(q\ell)^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q\ell)^\times$.
--
--   Fix further a discrete valuation ring $A$ which is a domain, Henselian local, with algebraically closed residue field, equipped with an $A$-algebra structure on $L$ making $L$ the fraction field of $A$, and an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with that of $L$; assume $q \in \mathfrak m_A$ (`hAq`) and that $\xi$ lies in the image of $A$ (`hξA`). Fix a nonzero $j \in K$ whose Laurent series is [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81), where [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) $=$ `HahnSeries.single (-1) 1` times the power series `jNumQ`, i.e. the $q$-expansion of the modular $j$-invariant. Fix $\varpi$ generating $\mathfrak m_A$ (`hϖ`) and $\varpi_t \in A$ with $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q\,u$ for some unit $u$ (`hϖt`).
--
--   Write $C :=$ `chartAlgFin A ↥K j`, the $A$-subalgebra `chartAlg A ↥K {j}` of $K$ attached to the singleton $\{j\}$, with distinguished element `jChartFin A ↥K j` $= j$; write $X :=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A ↥K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) for the scheme obtained as the pushout of the two chart morphisms `fFin`, `fInf`, with structure morphism `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec} A$ and with `ιFin` $\colon \operatorname{Spec} C \to X$ the finite chart.
--
--   **The point $y$.** An ideal $y$ of $C$ is given, maximal (`hy`), containing the image of $\varpi$ (`hϖy`), and supersingular in the sense of `hss`: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi \colon C \to \Omega$ with kernel $y$, the element $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), that is, every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has no nonzero point annihilated by $q$.
--
--   **The rigidity hypothesis `hArig`.** This hypothesis asserts, for every point $z$ of $X$ such that the germ at $z$ of the global section of $X$ obtained from $\varpi$ along `toBase` lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$, and every point $y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ with `ιFin` $(y') = z$ whose ideal satisfies the same supersingularity condition as `hss`, the existence of: a complete discrete valuation domain $W$, a ring homomorphism $\sigma \colon A \to W$ with $\mathfrak m_W = (\sigma\varpi)$, power series $f, u, v \in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u, v$ units and $f - (X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1) \in (X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$ (the subtracted term being [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.drinfeldForm q W`](def/DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart.html#L18)), and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the adic completion of $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ at its maximal ideal onto $S := W[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(\sigma(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))\,v - f\,u)$, subject to seven clauses, summarised here: (i) $e$ carries the image in the completion of the germ of a constant $a \in A$ to the class of $C(\sigma a)$; (ii) for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, every $L$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ with [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L (q*ℓ) ξ (q*ℓ) ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (levelH (q*ℓ) M') γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29) — the condition that, for all weights $k$, all modular forms $f_1,g_1$ of level `GammaH ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (levelH (q*ℓ) M')` with integral $q$-expansions and $g_1$'s series nonzero, and all $x \in K$ whose Laurent series is the coefficientwise image of the quotient of those series, the image of $\tau x$ under any embedding $L \to \mathbb{C}$ sending $\xi$ to $\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$, multiplied by the $q$-expansion of $g_1 \mid_k$ (the level-$(q\ell)$ conjugate of $\gamma^{-1}$), equals the $q$-expansion of $f_1 \mid_k$ of the same conjugate — maps $C$ into $C$; (iii) for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M') \cap \Gamma(\ell)$ such a $\tau$ restricted to $C$ is congruent to the identity modulo $y'$; (iv) for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and such a $\tau$ preserving $C$ and trivial modulo $y'$ there are a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, an element $c \in W$ and a matrix $M \in \mathrm{M}_2(W)$ with $\theta$ intertwining $\Psi$ with the restriction of $\tau$, $\theta$ fixing classes of constants, $\theta(X_j) \equiv \sum_i C(M_{ij})X_i$ modulo the square of the ideal generated by the classes of $X_0,X_1$, $c^{q+1} \equiv 1$, $M_{ij} \equiv c\,\gamma_{ij}$ modulo $\mathfrak m_W$, $c \equiv 1$ when $\gamma \in \Gamma(\ell)$, and $c \not\equiv 1$ when $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau$ is not the identity; (v) primes of $S$ not containing both classes of $X_0,X_1$, containing the class of $C(\sigma\varpi)$, and containing elements with linear parts $a_iX_0+b_iX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^2$ with $q \nmid a_1b_2-a_2b_1$, have distinct contractions to $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$; (vi) for a prime $P$ of $S$ as in (v) whose linear part may be taken to be $X_0$, the germ of $a \in C$ lies in the contraction of $P$ along $e$ precisely when every Laurent coefficient of $a$ lies in the image of $\mathfrak m_A$; (vii) [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L (q*ℓ)`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) lies in $K$ and in $C$, and after subtracting a suitable $a_0 \in A$ (with the difference in $y'$) its image under $e$ is the class of some $h \in (X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$, $e_0 \ge 1$, whose degree-$e_0$ form takes unit values at all $(a,b) \in W^2$ not both in $\mathfrak m_W$ with $a^qb-ab^q \in \mathfrak m_W$.
--
--   **The chosen point and the chosen witness.** A point $z$ of $X$ is fixed together with $\varpi_z$, the germ at $z$ of the section coming from $\varpi$ along `toBase` (`hϖz`), assumed to lie in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ (`hz`); a point $y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ with `ιFin` $(y') = z$ (`hy'`) is fixed, satisfying the supersingularity condition `hss'`, and with $y'$'s ideal equal to $y$ (`hy'y`). Data $W_1, \sigma_1, f_1, u_1, v_1, e_1$ of the kind produced by `hArig` are fixed: $W_1$ a complete discrete valuation domain, $\sigma_1 \colon A \to W_1$ with $\mathfrak m_{W_1} = (\sigma_1\varpi)$, $u_1, v_1$ units, $f_1 - (X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1) \in (X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and $e_1$ a ring isomorphism from the adic completion of $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ onto $S := W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))v_1 - f_1u_1)$; the hypothesis `hW₁` asserts for this data exactly the seven clauses (i)–(vii) listed above, with $W_1,\sigma_1,e_1$ in place of $W,\sigma,e$ and with the fixed $z$, $y'$.
--
--   Finally an ideal $J$ of $C$ is given which, by `hJ`, is the infimum of the set of ideals of the form $\mathrm{comap}_{\tau|_C}\bigl(\mathrm{comap}_{\Psi}(\,(\,\mathrm{mk}_S(C(\sigma_1\varpi_t)),\ \mathrm{mk}_S(X_0),\ \mathrm{mk}_S(X_1)\,)\,)\bigr)$, taken over all $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and all $L$-algebra automorphisms $\tau$ of $K$ satisfying `IsLevelAutAt` for $\gamma^{-1}$ as above and mapping $C$ into $C$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Write $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ for the stalk at $z$, $\mathrm{toC}$ for the canonical map from $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ to its adic completion at the maximal ideal, $\mathrm{mk}_S$ for the quotient map $W_1[[X_0,X_1]] \to S$, $\mathrm{germY} \colon C \to \mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ for the germ at $z$ taken through the finite chart (the inverse of the global-sections comparison for $\operatorname{Spec} C$, followed by the inverse of the chart isomorphism for `ιFin` on $\top$, followed by the germ at $z$ on the image open set), and $\Psi := e_1 \circ \mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germY} \colon C \to S$. Then both of the following hold.
--
--   First, the ideal of $S$ generated by $\Psi(y)$ is $\bigl(\mathrm{mk}_S(C(\sigma_1\varpi)),\ \mathrm{mk}_S(X_0),\ \mathrm{mk}_S(X_1)\bigr)$.
--
--   Second, for every natural number $n$, the contraction along $\Psi$ of the $n$-th power of that ideal $\bigl(\mathrm{mk}_S(C(\sigma_1\varpi)),\ \mathrm{mk}_S(X_0),\ \mathrm{mk}_S(X_1)\bigr)^n$ equals $y^n$.
--
--   This is the local comparison at a supersingular point of the two-chart integral model: the chart map $\Psi$ into the Drinfeld local presentation $S$ carries the supersingular maximal ideal $y$ onto the maximal ideal $(\sigma_1\varpi, X_0, X_1)$ of $S$ and induces an exact matching of the two $\mathfrak m$-adic filtrations, $\Psi^{-1}(\mathfrak m_S^n) = y^n$. It feeds the construction of the blow-up chart comparison isomorphism in [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_ringHom_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_blowupChartAt_localChart_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_ringHom_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_blowupChartAt_localChart_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked), and is proved from the companion statements on contraction, density and flatness, on stability of the centre under level automorphisms, and on the image of the orbit centre.
